Upstream attribution
--------------------
The mathematical content in papers/ is derived from the preprints in the public
openai/math repository (https://github.com/openai/math), which is distributed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The upstream repository describes the
manuscripts as produced by an internal OpenAI model and as being at different
stages of verification; it lists no per-paper human authors, so none are given
here and none are invented. Each paper keeps its original title, source slug and
date. The upstream repository has no NOTICE file at its root (checked on
2026-10-19), so there is no upstream NOTICE text to retain beyond its LICENSE,
which is copied unchanged. This project is not affiliated with and is not
endorsed by OpenAI.

Statement of changes
--------------------
The papers were modified. Section 7 of each paper is the upstream paper converted
from TeX to Markdown, with citation markers, cross-reference links, label
anchors, bibliography entries and figure descriptions restored by recorded
insertions. Sections 0 to 6, 8, 9 and 10 were added and are generated or
assembled as marked: reading maps, result contracts, definitions and bounds,
proof roadmaps, engineering and domain contracts, applicability limits, graph
links, verification records and structured metadata blocks. Catalogues
(catalogue/, Catalogo_Math.md) were added.

The following were added and are original to this repository: the router
(tools/route_v2.py and the index builder, evaluation and gate tools), its
vocabulary, thesaurus and parameters (standards/, out/params.json), the built
index (out/index), the evaluation benchmark (eval/, test_eval/) and the measured
results. Generated interpretation is identified separately from the original
text; this notice makes no independent correctness claim.
